{{also|byt|byť|by't}}
==Czech==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|cs|sla-pro|*byti}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|cs}} {{m|ine-pro|*bʰuH-||to become}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/biːt/|lang=cs}}
* {{audio|Cs-být.ogg|audio|lang=cs}}
* {{homophones|bít|lang=cs}}

===Verb===
{{cs-verb|a=i}}

# to [[be]]
#: {{uxi|cs|Ten kabát je vlhký|The coat is wet.}}
# to [[be]] {{gloss|to exist}}
# {{lb|cs|auxiliary}} {{non-gloss definition|Present forms are used in combination with [[past participle]]s to form [[past tense]].}}
#: {{uxi|cs|Jel '''jsem''' do Prahy.|I went to Prague.}}
# {{lb|cs|auxiliary}} {{non-gloss definition|Future forms are used in combination with [[infinitive]]s of other verbs to form their [[future tense]].}}
#: {{uxi|cs|'''Budu''' ti pomáhat.|I will be helping you.}}
# {{lb|cs|auxiliary}} {{non-gloss definition|Conditional forms are used only to form the [[conditional mood]] with combination of a verb's past participles.}}
#: {{uxi|cs|Já '''bych''' to neudělal.|I would not do it.}}
# {{lb|cs|auxiliary}} {{non-gloss definition|Used in combination with [[passive participles]] of other verbs to form their [[passive voice]].}}
#: {{uxi|cs|'''Jsem''' překvapen.|I am surprised.}}
# {{lb|cs|auxiliary}} {{non-gloss definition|Past participle forms of "být" are used in combination with conditional forms of "být" and past participles of other verbs to form their [[past conditional]].}}
#: {{uxi|cs|'''Byl''' by tam šel, kdyby ho '''byli''' pozvali.|He would have gone there if they had invited him.}}

